    <h2>Los Angeles to Fresno — FAQ</h2>
    <div class="faq"><h3>How much is a carpool from Los Angeles to Fresno?</h3><p>Seat prices usually run $25–$40 per seat. You're splitting the driver's real fuel and wear cost — capped at the IRS mileage rate — so there's no surge pricing and no markup.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><h3>How long is the drive from Los Angeles to Fresno?</h3><p>About 3.5–4 hours, covering roughly 220 miles depending on traffic and stops.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><h3>What is the cheapest way to get from Los Angeles to Fresno?</h3><p>A carpool seat is usually the cheapest door-to-door option at $25–$40. Driving yourself costs about $35 in fuel alone (220 miles at 30 mpg and $4.80/gallon, before parking and wear), and that's before you split it with anyone. Bus and train fares change daily and are usually slower; flying can win on cost if you book early, but rarely once you add three hours of airport at either end. Prices checked July 2026.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><h3>Is a carpool cheaper than driving alone, the bus, or flying Los Angeles to Fresno?</h3><p>For most trips, yes on the all-in cost. At $25–$40 you split fuel instead of paying for a full tank (~$35 for this route), you skip airport time, bag fees and transit transfers, and you get dropped closer to where you're actually going.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><h3>Can I bring luggage or a snowboard?</h3><p>Yes. Add a note when you book (for example "1 suitcase" or "a snowboard") so the driver can plan trunk space.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><h3>Where do pickups and drop-offs happen?</h3><p>Drivers pick a spot that works for the route. Common Los Angeles areas include Downtown LA, Westwood/UCLA, Santa Monica, Pasadena and the Valley; on the Fresno end, Downtown Fresno, Clovis and Fresno State. You confirm the exact spot in the app after booking.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><h3>Do I get charged when I request a ride?</h3><p>No. On a request-to-book ride your card is only authorized — you're charged when the driver accepts. If they decline, don't respond, or you withdraw first, nothing is charged. So you can send a request with a question ("can you leave after 6pm?") and the driver reads it before any money moves.</p></div>
<div class="faq"><h3>Is Seat Sherpa safe?</h3><p>Every driver is ID- and license-verified, your payment is held securely until your trip starts (you share a pickup code with the driver), and riders and drivers rate each other after every trip. Everyone is 18+.</p></div>
